<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">First Austrian Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1934 CE · capital Vienna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Inter-war Austrian democracy, a small state left by the Habsburg collapse that slid into civil war and dictatorship.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-german-austria">Republic of German-Austria</a> was renamed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-austria">Republic of Austria</a> in October 1919 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saint-germain-en-laye-1919">Treaty of Saint-Germain</a> forbade union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. The federal constitution of 1920, drafted with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hans-kelsen">Hans Kelsen</a>, created a federal parliamentary republic; with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgenland">Burgenland</a> added in 1921 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> separated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a> in 1922, it had nine states.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was polarised between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-social-party-austria">Christian Social Party</a>, strong in the countryside, and the Social Democrats of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-vienna">Red Vienna</a>, who built large council housing estates. Each side had armed militias. Chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ignaz-seipel">Ignaz Seipel</a> stabilised the currency with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> loan in 1922. The burning of the Palace of Justice in 1927 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Depression</a> deepened the crisis.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In March 1933 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/engelbert-dollfuss">Chancellor Engelbert Dollfuss</a> suspended parliament. After a brief civil war in February 1934 the Social Democrats were banned, and the May 1934 constitution created the authoritarian <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-state-of-austria">Federal State of Austria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/first-austrian-republic.jpg" alt="First Austrian Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: SpinnerLaserzthe2nd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Austria_(1230%E2%80%931934,_1945%E2%80%932000).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1934 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vienna</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Karl Renner, Ignaz Seipel, Engelbert Dollfuss</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Austria (1919-1934)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=first-austrian-republic" aria-label="First Austrian Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5061 491 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where First Austrian Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5381 747L5379 775M5381 747L5381 747M5381 747L5381 747M5381 747L5381 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5379 775h0M5381 747h0M5381 747h0M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5381 747h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vienna. <a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=first-austrian-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
